WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.492
A café raises checklists and repairs, while a new-store project needs milestones and punch items. In this video, you’ll choose which ticket types each work area can use.

2
00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:24.833
In Work Configuration, open Ticket Type Mapping. Your work areas are grouped under Projects, Operations for your locations, and Approvals. Each one lists the ticket types people can create there.

3
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.593
Bayview opening is the new café being built. Let’s let the team there order supplies too. Click the plus.

4
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:38.732
Tick every type this work area should offer. You can search, or select them all. Nothing changes until you save.

5
00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:46.228
Save, and supplier orders now show up for Bayview opening. To take a type away, click the cross on it, then save.

6
00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:52.320
Removing a type only stops new tickets of that type. Tickets already created stay as they are.

7
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:59.479
Now, when someone creates a ticket and picks Bayview opening, Supplier Order is one of the types they can choose.

8
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:09.585
That’s ticket type mapping. Next in the Admin console series: approval types. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

